.TH PATH_IS_ROOT 3
.SH NAME
path_is_root \- check if a path refers to the filesystem root
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <path.h>
.PP
.BI "int path_is_root(const char* " p ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B path_is_root
determines whether the given path
.I p
refers to the root directory of the filesystem.
.PP
The implementation is platform-specific:
.TP
.B Windows
Uses the Windows API function
.BR PathIsRootW
to verify if the path represents a drive root (e.g., "C:\").
.TP
.B POSIX
Compares the device and inode numbers of the directory
.I p
with those of its parent directory (".."). If the device and inode match,
.I p
is considered the root of the filesystem.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.TP
.B 1
The path is the root of the filesystem.
.TP
.B 0
The path is not the root.
.TP
.B -1
An error occurred (e.g., the path could not be accessed using
.BR lstat (2)).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lstat (2),
.BR path_canonical (3)